  </p>

  <h2>1. Who We Are</h2>
  <p>
    Pereste Health Inc. (“<strong>Pereste</strong>,” “<strong>we</strong>,” “<strong
      >us</strong
    >,” “<strong>our</strong>”) is a Louisiana corporation that builds the
    Hearth mobile application (“<strong>Hearth</strong>” or the “<strong
      >App</strong
    >”). Hearth is a patient-companion app that partner healthcare clinics (“<strong
      >Clinics</strong
    >”) offer to their patients to support chronic-condition care, education, and
    visit preparation.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Contact:</strong><br />
    Pereste Health Inc., Louisiana, USA<br />
    Email: <a href="mailto:parker@pereste.com">parker@pereste.com</a>
  </p>

  <h2>2. Important Framing — How Hearth Fits in Your Care</h2>
  <p>
    Hearth is offered to you <strong>through your Clinic</strong>, not directly
    by Pereste to the public. Your Clinic is a HIPAA Covered Entity. <strong
      >Pereste is a HIPAA Business Associate of your Clinic</strong
    > under a Business Associate Agreement (“BAA”).
  </p>
  <p>This means:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>For your Protected Health Information (“PHI”)</strong> — including
      information about your conditions, medications, lab and vital-sign
      readings, allergies, and conversations with the App’s voice
      assistant — your Clinic’s <strong>Notice of Privacy Practices</strong> governs
      how that information may be used and disclosed. Pereste handles that PHI on
      your Clinic’s behalf, only as permitted by the BAA and this Privacy Policy.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>For non-PHI information</strong> — such as App usage analytics,
      device crash signals, and account-management data — this Privacy Policy
      describes Pereste’s own practices.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If you have questions about how your Clinic uses your health information,
    contact your Clinic directly. If you have questions about Hearth itself,
    contact Pereste at <a href="mailto:parker@pereste.com">parker@pereste.com</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Who Can Use Hearth</h2>
  <p>
    Hearth is intended for <strong>adults aged 18 or older</strong> who have been
    enrolled by a participating Clinic. Hearth is not directed to children under
    18, and we do not knowingly collect information from anyone under 18 through
    the App. If you believe a person under 18 has used Hearth, contact us at <a
      href="mailto:parker@pereste.com">parker@pereste.com</a
    > and we will work with the relevant Clinic to address it.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Information We Collect</h2>

  <h3>4.1 Information you provide directly</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Enrollment code.</strong> A short, single-use code issued to you by
      your Clinic. Used once to register your device.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Patient profile.</strong> Your first name, last name, age,
      pronouns, list of conditions, list of allergies. Your Clinic may provide
      some of this information; you may edit it in the App.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Health readings and check-ins you enter.</strong> Lab and
      vital-sign readings relevant to your conditions (for example, blood sugar,
      blood pressure, weight, oxygen level, and kidney-function values), symptom
      and mood check-ins, and medications you record or mark as taken.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Voice input.</strong> When you speak to the App, audio is captured
      to power the voice assistant.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Settings and preferences.</strong> Auto-lock interval, voice persona,
      language, accessibility settings.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Apple Health data you choose to connect (optional).</strong> If you
      turn on the Apple Health connection, Hearth reads only the specific health
      readings you authorize — such as blood glucose, blood pressure, weight,
      oxygen level, and peak flow — so they appear alongside the rest of your
      information. Hearth reads these only from your device, does not write
      anything back to Apple Health, and never uses this data for advertising.
      You can turn the connection off at any time in iOS Settings or in the App.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>4.2 Information we receive from your Clinic and connected systems</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Clinical record (FHIR Bundle).</strong> Your Clinic’s electronic
      medical record system (“EMR”) provides an HL7 FHIR R4 bundle representing
      portions of your clinical record — conditions, medications, lab results,
      demographics, visit history, care team — so the App can show it to you and
      personalize content.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>4.3 Information collected automatically</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Device-paired authentication keys.</strong> When you enroll, the
      App generates a P-256 cryptographic key pair inside your iPhone’s <strong
        >Secure Enclave</strong
      >. The private key never leaves your device. The public key is sent to our
      servers so we can verify that requests come from your device.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Apple App Attest assertion.</strong> During enrollment, the App
      requests an attestation from Apple’s App Attest service to prove that an
      unmodified copy of Hearth is running on a genuine Apple device. The
      assertion is sent to our servers.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Session bearer token.</strong> After enrollment, our servers issue
      a bearer token stored in the iOS Keychain on your device (configured so it
      cannot sync to iCloud or to another device).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>App analytics events.</strong> Pereste’s first-party analytics
      layer records de-identified, aggregate events — for example, “screen
      viewed,” “lesson started,” “medication reminder scheduled” — to operate,
      debug, and improve the App. These events are filtered through a strict
      allow-list so that no PHI (such as raw A1C values, blood-sugar values,
      names, or conversation text) is attached to them.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Diagnostic information.</strong> Anonymous error counts and
      performance timings (no transcript or PHI text content).
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>4.4 Information we do <em>not</em> collect</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      We do <strong>not</strong> include third-party advertising SDKs, advertising
      identifiers, Firebase, or third-party analytics services such as Google Analytics,
      Amplitude, Mixpanel, or similar.
    </li>
    <li>
      We do <strong>not</strong> include third-party crash-reporting services such
      as Crashlytics, Sentry, or Bugsnag.
    </li>
    <li>
      We do <strong>not</strong> track you across other companies’ apps or websites
      for advertising purposes.
    </li>
    <li>We do <strong>not</strong> sell your personal information.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. iOS Permissions Hearth Requests</h2>
  <p>
    When you use specific features, iOS will prompt you for permission. You can
    change these in <strong>Settings → Hearth</strong> at any time.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Permission</th><th>Why Hearth uses it</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr
        ><td>Microphone</td><td>Capture your voice when you tap the voice button.</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td>Speech Recognition</td><td
          >Convert your speech to text so the App can understand what you said.</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td>Face ID</td><td
          >Unlock the App after auto-lock. Hearth never sees your face data; iOS
          handles the match locally.</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td>Notifications</td><td
          >Deliver medication reminders and visit reminders you’ve enabled.</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td>Apple Health</td><td
          >Read the health readings you choose to share (such as glucose, blood
          pressure, weight, and oxygen level) so they appear in Hearth. Hearth
          does not write to Apple Health.</td
        ></tr
      >
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    You may use Hearth without granting Microphone or Speech Recognition; you
    will not be able to use the voice assistant in that case.
  </p>

  <h2>6. How Speech-to-Text Works</h2>
  <p>
    Hearth uses Apple’s <strong>Speech Recognition</strong> framework to convert
    your spoken words into text. On a supported iPhone, Hearth requires <strong
      >on-device recognition</strong
    >, so your audio is processed entirely on your device and is <strong
      >not sent to Apple’s servers</strong
    >. If on-device recognition is not available on your device, Hearth will not
    fall back to cloud recognition for that request.
  </p>
  <p>The resulting transcript text is treated as PHI and follows Section 7.</p>

  <h2>7. How We Use Your Information</h2>
  <p>We use the information described in Section 4 to:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>Provide the App.</strong> Authenticate your device, show you your clinical
      record, run the voice assistant, deliver lessons and reminders, and let you
      record check-ins.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Personalize content.</strong> Tailor lessons, prompts, and reminders
      to your conditions, medications, and prior interactions.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Operate the voice assistant.</strong> Convert your speech to text,
      generate a response using Pereste’s self-hosted language model, and play the
      response back through Pereste’s self-hosted text-to-speech engine.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Communicate with your Clinic</strong> as permitted by your Clinic’s
      BAA and Notice of Privacy Practices — for example, surfacing a Clinic-authored
      care plan or returning summary data to the EMR.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Maintain security.</strong> Detect device tampering, rate-limit abuse,
      sign requests, verify device identity, and respond to incidents.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Improve Hearth.</strong> Analyze de-identified, aggregate analytics
      to find bugs and improve usability.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Comply with law.</strong> Respond to lawful requests and meet HIPAA,
      state, and other legal obligations.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>8. Where Your Information Goes</h2>

  <h3>8.1 On-premises processing</h3>
  <p>
    A defining design choice for Hearth: <strong
      >PHI does not leave Pereste’s on-premises stack</strong
    > for processing by external cloud providers. Our backend services, language
    model, and text-to-speech engine are operated by Pereste on infrastructure we
    control.
  </p>

  <h3>8.2 Service providers we do use</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Apple Inc.</strong> — App distribution through the App Store, push
      notifications via APNs, App Attest attestation, on-device Speech
      Recognition framework, Face ID. Apple’s own privacy policy applies to
      these services.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your Clinic and its EMR vendor</strong> — receive and may store information
      we send back on your Clinic’s behalf, per your Clinic’s Notice of Privacy Practices.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Our infrastructure providers</strong> — for example, the
      data-center / colocation and network providers that host Pereste’s stack —
      under written contracts that include HIPAA Business-Associate terms where
      they may access PHI.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do <strong>not</strong> transfer your PHI to advertising networks, marketing
    platforms, or generative-AI cloud providers.
  </p>

  <h3>8.3 Disclosures permitted by law</h3>
  <p>
    We may disclose information if required by subpoena, court order, or other
    legal process; to investigate fraud or security threats; to protect the
    rights, property, or safety of Pereste, our users, or others; or in
    connection with a corporate transaction such as a merger or acquisition (in
    which case, the acquirer will be bound by terms no less protective than this
    Privacy Policy with respect to your information).
  </p>

  <h3>8.4 Location of processing</h3>
  <p>
    Hearth is operated from the United States and intended for use in the United
    States.
  </p>

  <h2>9. How We Protect Your Information</h2>
  <p>
    Hearth applies the technical safeguards required by the HIPAA Security Rule
    (45 C.F.R. § 164.312) and a layered set of additional controls:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Encryption in transit.</strong> All authenticated traffic uses TLS
      with certificate pinning in release builds.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Encryption at rest on your device.</strong> Sensitive fields stored
      on your iPhone — including your patient profile and the cached copy of your
      clinical record (FHIR bundle) — are encrypted with ChaChaPoly, and the symmetric
      key is wrapped against a per-install key held in the Secure Enclave.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Device-bound authentication.</strong> P-256 keys in the Secure Enclave
      sign every request; bearer tokens are stored in the iOS Keychain with the strictest
      accessibility class (<code>WhenUnlockedThisDeviceOnly</code>) and do not sync
      to iCloud.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>App integrity.</strong> Apple App Attest is used to verify the App at
      enrollment.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Access controls.</strong> Face ID gate on launch and after idle timeout.
      App-switcher PHI screen-shield. Screen-recording overlay.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Administrative safeguards.</strong> Workforce training, least-privilege
      access, written policies, incident response, and BAAs with subcontractors who
      may handle PHI.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    No system is perfectly secure. If we learn of a breach of unsecured PHI, we
    will notify your Clinic, and your Clinic will notify you, in accordance with
    the HIPAA Breach Notification Rule (45 C.F.R. §§ 164.400–414) and applicable
    state law.
  </p>

  <h2>10. How Long We Keep Your Information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>PHI</strong> is retained per the retention schedule in your Clinic’s
      BAA and Notice of Privacy Practices.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Bearer tokens and device keys</strong> are retained until you sign out
      from a device, your Clinic revokes your access, or you uninstall the App.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Analytics</strong> are retained only on a de-identified, aggregate basis.
      We do not attach identifiers to analytics events.
    </li>
    <li>
      When the BAA between Pereste and your Clinic ends, Pereste will return or
      destroy PHI as required by 45 C.F.R. § 164.504(e)(2)(ii)(J), and as further
      specified in the BAA.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>11. Your Rights</h2>
  <p>
    Because your Clinic is the Covered Entity for your PHI, the HIPAA-based
    rights below run primarily through your Clinic. Pereste will support your
    Clinic in fulfilling them.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Access</strong> the PHI your Clinic holds about you (45 C.F.R. § 164.524).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Amend</strong> PHI you believe is inaccurate (45 C.F.R. § 164.526).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Receive an accounting of disclosures</strong> as required by HIPAA
      (45 C.F.R. § 164.528).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Request restrictions</strong> on certain uses and disclosures (45 C.F.R.
      § 164.522).
    </li>
    <li><strong>Receive notice of a breach</strong> of unsecured PHI.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>File a complaint</strong> with your Clinic, with Pereste at <a
        href="mailto:parker@pereste.com">parker@pereste.com</a
      >, or with the U.S. Department of Health and Human Services Office for
      Civil Rights.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise rights regarding PHI, <strong>contact your Clinic first.</strong>
    To exercise rights regarding non-PHI information held by Pereste, contact <a
      href="mailto:parker@pereste.com">parker@pereste.com</a
    >.
  </p>
  <h3>State privacy laws</h3>
  <p>
    Most state comprehensive privacy laws exempt PHI processed under HIPAA.
    Hearth’s current patients are enrolled by Louisiana clinics, and Louisiana
    has not enacted a comprehensive consumer-privacy law. If Hearth becomes
    available to patients in states with applicable consumer-privacy laws, we
    will update this section with the disclosures and rights those laws require.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Children’s Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Hearth is not intended for and is not directed to children under 18. We do
    not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13, and we do
    not knowingly collect personal information from minors between 13 and 17.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you believe we have collected information from someone under 18, contact <a
      href="mailto:parker@pereste.com">parker@pereste.com</a
    > and we will work with the relevant Clinic to delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2>
  <p>
    Hearth is a native iOS app and does not use cookies. The App stores small
    amounts of operational data — a bearer token, settings, encrypted PHI cache
    — locally on your device using the iOS Keychain and the App’s sandboxed
    storage. You can clear this data by signing out (in Settings) or by
    uninstalling the App.
  </p>
  <p>
    Pereste’s informational website (pereste.com), where this policy is
    published, is a static site and does not set advertising or tracking
    cookies.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we make material
    changes, we will:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>Update the “Last Updated” date at the top.</li>
    <li>
      Notify you through an in-App notice and, where required, by other
      reasonable means.
    </li>
    <li>
      Where required by law, obtain your renewed consent before the change
      applies to you.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    You can always find the current version inside the App and at <a
      href="https://pereste.com/privacy">pereste.com/privacy</a
    >.
  </p>

